		{
			"id": "115470678576147889",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@mattdarveniza/115470678548491108",
			"author": {
				"name": "Matt",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@mattdarveniza",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/775/696/788/594/094/original/452c34074d1fc5cc.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-10-31T20:32:06.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I have my devices switch from light to dark mode when it gets dark outside, but there are certain websites that I want to have a consistently light or dark theme. I’ll often switch away from auto to ensure those sites remain in one theme regardless of time of day</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115470715153699226",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://socel.net/@janowiak/115470715133237832",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jesse Janowiak",
				"url": "https://socel.net/@janowiak",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/115/363/293/732/444/127/original/12dc66de658dc712.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-10-31T20:41:25.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I haven’t done any research into this, but my sense is that the alternative is even more confusing to users, even though it appears simpler.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115470722414268368",
			"parentId": "115470715153699226",
			"url": "https://socel.net/@janowiak/115470722397017305",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jesse Janowiak",
				"url": "https://socel.net/@janowiak",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/115/363/293/732/444/127/original/12dc66de658dc712.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-10-31T20:43:15.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Possible user confusion from offering all three options: “Huh, I wonder why I would choose ‘light’ when it’s already light?” Worst-case outcome: they pick the one they actually want and it works like the expected.</p><p>Possible user confusion for offering only “auto” and the opposite of the current color: “Where is the ‘light’ option? I clicked on dark, and now I want to change it back but it looks like I can’t.” Worst-case outcome: minor frustration.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115470739262943264",
			"parentId": "115470722414268368",
			"url": "https://front-end.social/@sarajw/115470739227141103",
			"author": {
				"name": "Sara Joy :happy_pepper:",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@sarajw",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/297/809/026/408/317/original/97d986685a3ca9d3.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-10-31T20:47:32.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://socel.net/@janowiak\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>janowiak</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> or it works like a toggle, from the mode you're in to the opposite, and back again.</p><p>But that way you can never get back to auto, presumably.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115470812015196057",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@stegrainer/115470811680924363",
			"author": {
				"name": "Ste Grainer",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@stegrainer",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/616/132/169/089/783/original/f5974340e6258025.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-10-31T21:05:58.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I left auto in as the default because some people may choose to have light/dark mode change with time or environment. My picker (based on Richard Rutter’s) saves to localdata so I didn’t want to force sticking with whatever choice they had set the first time visiting.</p><p>I expect most users to stick with the default auto mode but provide a picker in case they don’t want to.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115470938380730058",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mas.to/@maxfenton/115470938364296887",
			"author": {
				"name": "Max Fenton",
				"url": "https://mas.to/@maxfenton",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/113/393/205/249/439/115/original/4a4276a22126faf2.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2025-10-31T21:38:11.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I always like giving a default/auto option in a CMS but on a front-end maybe it could just check prefs and default light/dark to that. Same if there’s a high-contrast toggle.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115470940912189167",
			"parentId": "115470739262943264",
			"url": "https://socel.net/@janowiak/115470940867980070",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jesse Janowiak",
				"url": "https://socel.net/@janowiak",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/115/363/293/732/444/127/original/12dc66de658dc712.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-10-31T21:38:49.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@sarajw\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>sarajw</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Exactly! The first time we implemented a dark/light toggle at my old job, we went around the possible implementations for quite a while before settling on the least-bad option.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115470948015473529",
