			},
			"date": "2025-10-31T21:40:38.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Sometimes I too go outside (with my laptop)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115470948856506348",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@fantinel/115470948825475486",
			"author": {
				"name": "Matt Fantinel",
				"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@fantinel",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/110/616/574/646/179/864/original/29bd09c8b97b4f80.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-10-31T21:40:50.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> some people (a lot) have no idea the system preference is a thing, and set dark mode individually because that’s the only way they know how.</p><p>Also I’ve had people in the past give me the feedback that they like their Windows in light mode, but prefer sites in dark mode.</p><p>Point being, users are weird</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115470970366461412",
			"parentId": "115470948015473529",
			"url": "https://sunny.garden/@knowler/115470970339877053",
